Sval: a tab moves between the windows of one private session

Each private window is a session of its own, and no tab moves between two of
them (private-window-sessions.patch). A Peek opened from a private window is
in that window's session and shares its jar, so its page can move into the
window it came from as a tab, and a tab its page opens can move into a Peek
of its own. The swap is refused only between windows whose jars differ.

diff --git a/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js b/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js
index d1d6c17a06..cfc031a795 100644
--- a/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js
+++ b/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js
@@ -6288,10 +6288,13 @@
         return false;
       }
 
-      // Sval: nor between two private windows, each a session of its own.
+      // Sval: nor between two private sessions. A private window and the
+      // Peeks opened from it are one session, with one jar (SvalPrivateJars).
       if (
         aOtherTab.documentGlobal != window &&
-        PrivateBrowsingUtils.isWindowPrivate(window)
+        PrivateBrowsingUtils.isWindowPrivate(window) &&
+        aOtherTab.documentGlobal.gBrowser.defaultUserContextId !=
+          this.defaultUserContextId
       ) {
         return false;
       }
